# Products API – REST Client
#
# Endpoints: /products
# Purpose:
# - Menu items that can be sold. Products belong to categories
#   and can have modifier groups for customization options.
#
# Auth / cookies:
# - If your API uses Better Auth cookie sessions, keep @cookieJar consistent across files.
# - Origin protection: include Origin + Referer headers on protected routes.
#
# Usage flow:
# 1) Run Auth login in auth.http (stores cookie in jar)
# 2) Run requests here (cookie is reused via the same jar name)
#
# Notes:
# - Replace {{productId}}, {{workstationId}} with UUIDs from responses.
# - If your API is mounted under /api, set @apiPrefix = /api

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@origin = http://localhost:3000
@cookieJar = betterauth

# If your server mounts routes under /api, set this to /api. Otherwise leave empty.
@apiPrefix = /api

# IDs (paste values from responses)
@productId = d34ee699-bd21-44d9-9d55-cd6f43bf0f10
@workstationId = 


### List all products - ok
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/products
Origin: {{origin}}
Referer: {{origin}}/

### Retrieve a product by id - ok
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/products/{{productId}}
Origin: {{origin}}
Referer: {{origin}}/

### Search products by name - ok
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/products/search?query=burger
Origin: {{origin}}
Referer: {{origin}}/

//TODO: Flatten the response - missing dependencies | Not sure if we need this endpoint
###  Retrieve a product with its modifier groups and modifiers - ok
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/products/{{productId}}/modifiers
Origin: {{origin}}
Referer: {{origin}}/

//TODO: Flatten the response
###  Retrieve a product with full details (detailed)- ok
# Returns product with workstation, categories, modifier groups, modifiers, dependencies, and offers
# Designed for POS and admin detail views
GET {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/products/{{productId}}/detailed
Origin: {{origin}}
Referer: {{origin}}/


### Create a basic product - ok
POST {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}
Referer: {{origin}}/

{
  "name": "Capucino",
  "description": "Capucino",
  "basePrice": 450,
  "isActive": true
}

